          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em Lie 2-group
            is the generalization of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groups"} 2-groups
          %p
            it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+2-group"} smooth 2-group
            that happens to have a model given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            (in general only up to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          %p
            One general way to make the notion precise is as a special case of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"} 1-truncated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            object in
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
          %p
            these are
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
          %p
            Special cases of this have simpler definitions. For instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            is a model for a strict and comparatively tame Lie 2-group.
          %p
            Analogous to how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is in particular a Lie 2-group with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                as its space of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+infinity-groupoid"} discrete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"} 2-group
                is a Lie 2-group equipped with
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete smooth structure
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                there is a Lie 2-group denoted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \to 1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                as its space of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = U(1)
                the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
                is the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle 2-group
                \.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                of Lie groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo →
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \to G )
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to Aut(H)
                gives an example of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict
                Lie 2-group, using the general relation between crossed modules and
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
              %p
                For instance the crossed module
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(n) \to O(n)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U(1) \to 1)
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi String
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String(G)
                has various different but equivalent incarnations as a Lie 2-group. One is given by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo *
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mo *
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \Omega_* G \to P_* G
                internal to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frechet+manifold"} Frechet
                Lie groups.
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+infinity-group"} automorphism infinity-group
                is a smooth 2-group.
          %h2#constructions_and_applications Constructions and Applications
          %h3#DeloopingLie2Groupoid Delooping 2-groupoids
          %p
            By the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-groupoid"} Lie 2-groupoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_0
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            is given by the group product.
          %h3#principal_2bundles Principal 2-bundles
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            (or itself a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            such as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g : X \to \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a{:href => "#DeloopingLie2Groupoid"} delooping Lie 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            classify smooth
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi AUT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = AUT(H)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+2-group"} automorphism 2-group
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            then these are equivalently smooth
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Notice that a morphism of smooth
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}G
            is presented by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-anafunctor"} 2-anafunctor
            of 2-groupoid valued presheaves, given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  C(U_i) &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\simeq}
                  \\\
                  X
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(U_i)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+nerve"} Cech nerve
            2-groupoid of some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
            with coefficients in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"}> group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-group"}> 2-group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong Lie 2-group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-groupoid"} Lie 2-groupoid
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+2-group"} Poisson Lie 2-group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"}> ∞-group
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-group"} smooth ∞-group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth ∞-groupoid
          %h2#references References
          %p A first exposition is in the lecture notes
          %ul
            %li
              Alissa Crans,
              %em A survey of higher Lie theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://myweb.lmu.edu/acrans/SurveyHigherLieTheory.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A general review of Lie 2-groups, as well as a discussion of the example of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              , Alissa Crans,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              %em From Loop Groups to 2-Groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0504123"}> arXiv:math/0504123
              )
          %p Discussion in a more comprehensive context is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p with an introduction in section 1.3.1 and a general abstract discussion in 3.3.2.
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of Lie 2-groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gr%C3%A9gory+Ginot"}> Grégory Ginot
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ping+Xu"} Ping Xu
                %em Cohomology of Lie 2-groups
                (
                %a{:href => "http://people.math.jussieu.fr/~ginot/papers/CohLie2gp.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Wockel"}> Christoph Wockel
                ,
                %em Categorified central extensions, étale Lie 2-groups and Lieʼs Third Theorem for locally exponential Lie algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001870811002313"}> web
                )
            %li
